From: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 19:03:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(gridforge): capacity envelope engine, provenance system
 and reference study

Additive first patch. Adds a self-contained engineering core that answers the
commercial question the business is built on: how much AI compute can this hall
carry, what binds first, and what does each step of density cost.

- gridforge/validation: Quantity carrying a provenance DAG and an evidence class
  (E0-E7). Arithmetic propagates provenance and takes the minimum class, so a
  model applied to measured data yields a modelled number, never a measurement.
  Minimal unit algebra so racks * EUR/rack cancels to EUR and kW cannot be added
  to euros.
- gridforge/{site,power,compute,thermal}: input schemas and 13 independent
  constraint functions across electrical, thermal and physical domains, each
  returning the racks it permits, its basis, and what relief costs and takes.
- gridforge/envelope: the solver and the Headroom Ladder - relieve the binding
  constraint, solve again, repeat. The ladder is the customer-facing artefact.
- gridforge/scenario, gridforge/economics: scenarios as data, one-at-a-time
  sensitivity on the relieved case, AACE Class 5 screening economics.
- gridforge/reporting: typed report model that rejects bare numerals, CI gates
  that fail on missing provenance, on an evidence class above its inputs, on
  language asserting measurement over a modelled quantity, and - in ISSUED mode -
  on any capacity claim below its evidence floor.
- gridforge/integrations: ports for ThermalForge, DERIM and GridOS. Nothing
  implemented. A test fails the build if a domain module imports them.
- examples/reference_site.py: the exemplary synthetic reference project, four
  architectures compared, every page watermarked as synthetic.
- docs/: commercial spine, product spec, engineering assumption library, target
  architecture, market evidence log, patch notes.

No third-party dependencies, enforced by test. 28 tests pass.

Not yet reconciled against the audit of GridForge-AI, ThermalForge-Liquid-Cooling,
DERIM and GridOS - session-level repository access was unavailable. Where existing
code already does this and works, the existing code wins and this patch is trimmed.

